## SVG Mechanism: Webhook Delivery Pipeline

This standalone, zero-dependency HTML file renders an animated 2D architecture diagram of a webhook delivery pipeline (`Producer -> Queue -> Worker`) with a failed-delivery branch to `Retry DLQ`. No project `design/tokens.css` or `tokens.css` file was found in the workspace, so the page defines self-contained `design/tokens.css`-compatible light and dark CSS custom properties (`:root`, `:root[data-theme="dark"]`, and `@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)`) and binds every SVG `fill`, `stroke`, and `stop-color` exclusively to CSS variables, `url(#...)`, or `none`.

### Stages & Token Map

- **Stages & branches (exact user scope):**
  1. **Producer** (`Step 1`): Emits webhook events along the primary track (`Event`) into `Queue`.
  2. **Queue** (`Step 2`): Buffers event jobs and forwards them along the primary track (`Dispatch`) to `Worker`.
  3. **Worker** (`Step 3`): Consumes queued events for webhook delivery and routes failed deliveries down the warning branch (`Failed delivery`).
  4. **Retry DLQ** (`Branch`): Receives failed deliveries from `Worker`.
- **SVG token bindings (zero raw hex inside `<svg>`):**
  - Canvas & grid: `--mech-canvas` (`--color-surface-default`), `--mech-grid-dot` & `--mech-border` (`--color-border-default`).
  - Primary nodes & pills: `--mech-node-top` (`--color-surface-raised`), `--mech-node-bottom` (`--color-surface-subtle`), `--mech-node-border` (`--color-border-strong`), `--mech-pill-bg` (`--color-surface-raised`).
  - Primary tracks, arrows & signals: `--mech-track` (`--color-border-strong`), `--mech-accent` (`--color-action-primary-bg`), `--mech-accent-bg` (`--color-accent-subtle`).
  - Failed-delivery branch & Retry DLQ: `--mech-warn` (`--color-warning-text`), `--mech-warn-top` (`--color-warning-surface`), `--mech-warn-bottom` & `--mech-warn-bg` (`--color-warning-subtle`).
  - Typography & focus: `--mech-text` (`--color-text-default`), `--mech-muted` (`--color-text-muted`), `--mech-focus` (`--color-border-focus`).

